# ── ai-trader — repository-level environment reference ────────────────────
#
# This file used to describe a PostgreSQL + DATABASE_URL + Redis-PubSub
# architecture with a standalone WebSocket service. None of that exists any
# more: the datastore is MongoDB, the transport between the two backends is
# SQS, and WebSockets are served by the NestJS API itself.
#
# There is no process that reads this file. Each service loads its own .env:
#
#   ai-trader-signals/.env   <- copy from ai-trader-signals/.env.example
#                               Python / FastAPI / Celery. Market data,
#                               indicators, LLM signal generation, morning
#                               brief. Publishes signals to SQS. Port 8001.
#
#   ai-trader-api/.env       <- copy from ai-trader-api/.env.example
#                               NestJS. Auth, MongoDB, paper trading,
#                               watchlist, WebSocket gateway, SQS consumer.
#                               Port 8000.
#
#   ai-trader-frontend/.env.local  <- the NEXT_PUBLIC_* block below.
#                                     Next.js. Port 3000.
#
# docker-compose.yml wires the first two with `env_file:` and overrides the
# inter-service URLs to container hostnames, so the localhost defaults in the
# per-service examples are for running outside Docker.
#
# Keep this file as orientation only. Do not add service configuration here —
# it will not be read, and a variable that exists in two places diverges.

# ── Frontend (ai-trader-frontend/.env.local) ──────────────────────────────
# The only variables with no per-service example of their own.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000       # NestJS API base URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8000          # Socket.IO gateway — served by the API, not a separate service
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000       # this app's own public URL

# ── Not currently wired ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Web push (VAPID_*) and the broker integrations (DHAN_*, ZERODHA_*,
# ANGELONE_*) are declared in ai-trader-api/.env.example but their NestJS
# modules are empty stubs today. Left there rather than duplicated here.
